    "narrative": "Our offensive engine for today centers on **Corbin Carroll** (72.87) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13), our clear top-tier plays. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a prime matchup against Wrobleski; the combination of a favorable park and the opponent\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts his stolen base floor, making him our highest-upside asset. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** exploits a massive SP skill advantage against V\u00e1squez, R, with the platoon advantage and order spot pushing his efficiency well into the elite range. **Mickey Moniak** (71.00) rounds out our top trio, as his dynamic platoon edge against the right-handed McGreevy makes him a must-start despite a minor park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, who landed just outside our active threshold at 42.59. While he offers some utility against the left-handed Seymour, I, the SP\u2019s specific skill set suppressed his raw projection enough to favor the higher-ceiling outcomes of **Austin Riley** and **Josh Naylor**. Further down the board, **Zach McKinstry** failed to clear the 40.0 efficiency floor due to a poor lineup position and a stiff matchup against Webb, L, relegating him to the pine. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno** closely; while his 57.93 score is technically marginal, he remains our starting catcher, though he will need to navigate Wrobleski effectively to maintain his value.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given our heavy reliance on players facing the southpaw Miller, E\u2014specifically **Max Muncy**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Henry Bolte**. While Miller, E presents a winnable SP skill profile, the stacking of our lineup against him introduces variance. We are essentially betting on our ability to punish his inefficiency through favorable platoon splits and, in the case of **Henry Bolte**, the high-leverage opportunity provided by the leadoff spot. We continue to hold **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **James Wood** on the bench due to their respective IL designations, awaiting their return to help us make a late-season push in the SB category alongside **Jose Caballero**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Edwin Arroyo**.",
